cff-version: 1.0.0
title: "ShinyFPZ: A R Shiny app to aid in Functional Process Zone classification"
version: 1.0.0
license: "MIT"
type: software
abstract: "ShinyFPZ is an interactive R Shiny application for exploring and classifying Functional Process Zones (FPZs) from river network datasets using hydrogeomorphic variables obtained from the OpenRES QGIS plugin. The app provides a streamlined workflow for clustering river segments, visualizing results, and exporting both analytical and spatial outputs."
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - given-names: Jacob
    family-names: Nesslage
    affiliation: University of California, Merced
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9219-8365"
keywords:
  - functional process zone
  - riverine ecosystem synthesis
  - river classification
  - river ecology
  - stream ecology
  - hydrogeomorphology
